===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{linguistics}} The oldest known [[Slavonic]] [[alphabet]], designed around AD 862–863 by Saint [[Cyril]] in order to translate the [[Bible]] and other texts into [[Old Church Slavonic]]. Mostly replaced by [[Cyrillic]] alphabet in [[Orthodox Christian]] Slavic countries, but still in use in the Croatian Church along the [[Dalmatia]]n coast, in Czech and Croatian [[recension]]s of [[Church Slavic]].

====Synonyms====
* [[Glagolitic alphabet]]
* [[Glagolitsa]]
* {{qualifier|rare}} [[Bukvitsa]]
* {{qualifier|archaic}} [[Hieronymian]], [[Illyrian]], [[Slovenish]]

